{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "Using 2021 CKD-EPI Creatinine equation (no race).\n\nMale, age 66, Scr = 1.7 mg/dl.\n\nFor males: κ = 0.9, α = -0.302.\nScr/κ = 1.7/0.9 = 1.8889.\n\nSince Scr/κ > 1, use max term = 1.8889^(-1.200).\n\nCompute 1.8889^(-1.200):\nln(1.8889) = 0.6360\n× (-1.200) = -0.7632\nexp(-0.7632) = 0.4662\n\nAge factor: 0.9938^66.\nln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n× 66 = -0.41046\nexp(-0.41046) = 0.6634\n\nGFR = 142 × 0.4662 × 0.6634\n= 142 × 0.30928\n= 43.9\n\nFINAL: 44"}